why: run 16 wrote that this function asks about each scheme id without a settlement mode and returns true on a ledger that ignores the mode; what the function tells its caller, and why asking without a mode gives it, was reached only by reading the body and the caller; Kirill: the reader should not have to open the implementation to understand the comment, so a reader holding the block and the signature alone says the function tells whether the ledger has the scheme at all, whatever mode it reads, and that the warm-up needs this because the ledgers that stall are the ones that ignore the mode Rescored 2026-09-29 under §94: subject and phrasing keeps dropped, so its column no longer compares.
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
export async function claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(scheme: PostingScheme, formatName: string): Promise<boolean> {
  for (const schemeId of listSchemeIds(scheme)) {
    if ((await askScheme({ schemeId, formatName })) === LedgerClaim.Accepted) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
}
--- callers
// postings/warmup/PostingWarmUp.ts
export async function warmUpPosting(scheme: PostingScheme, formatName: string): Promise<void> {
  if (!(await claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(scheme, formatName))) {
    return;
  }

  await openPostingSession(scheme, formatName);
}
--- facts
A ledger that ignores the settlement mode stalls on its first posting under that scheme, and the warm-up in `postings/warmup/PostingWarmUp.ts` makes that first posting.
So this function asks about each scheme id without a settlement mode, and returns true on a ledger that ignores the mode.
